;; expect: main.f runnable no_l_identity
;; a row's constructor is its one runtime field on both readings. This body has no L reading
;; (it binds a match of a numeral under a constructor) and is the classifier's alone, which gives ByteArray.mk
;; and Array.mk the registry's row — the argument itself — as the typed route's erasure does
;; (row_types' `pack`): one table, so the two cannot disagree on a ByteArray's representation.
;; A row's constructor that takes a proof (Fin.mk) is refused there — nothing checks the proof
;; (dif_scope) — and so is a match that takes a row apart by another type's constructors
;; (row_e_match)
(fn f ((l (List UInt8))) ByteArray
  (let
    ((k Nat
       (match (List.cons 1 List.nil)
         ((List.cons 1 _) 1)
         (_ 0))))
    (ByteArray.mk (Array.mk l))))
